{"chunk_id":"809ad3","wall_time_seconds":2.4648826,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":637,"output":"{"query": "\"RenderSimpleLines\"", "count": 1, "results": [{"title": "v3.2.0 — clean line font for `simple`, keep `outline` as 3rd style, fix small-window toggle", "url": "https://github.com/aedneth/flowclock-cli/pull/16", "body": "## Summary\n\nFollow-up to v3.1.0 addressing two pieces of feedback on the `simple` display style:\n\n1. **`simple` was the wrong aesthetic.** v3.1.0 rendered `simple` as a hollow,\n   edge-traced *outline* of the block glyphs — busy and \"techy\", not the minimal\n   look intended. It's now a **clean heavy line font**: crisp seven-segment digits\n   in box-drawing strokes (`┏━┓ ┃ ┣━┫ ┗━┛`), minimal and airy, but scaled to the\n   same hero dimensions as `block` (shares the exact reserve-first geometry).\n2. **`d`-toggle looked broken on small / tiled windows.** Root cause: the old\n   outline coincided pixel-for-pixel with `block` at scale 1, so pressing `d` in a\n   small window changed nothing visible. The new line font differs from `block` at\n   **every** scale (including scale 1), so the toggle is always visible.\n\nPer request, the v3.1.0 hollow outline is **kept** as a third selectable style.\n\n## Styles (cycle `block → simple → outline` with `d`, or `display` in the `/` palette; all saved)\n\n- **`block`** (default, unchanged) — solid 7-segment glyphs.\n- **`simple`** — clean heavy box-drawing line digits.\n- **`outline`** — hollow, edge-traced block (the v3.1.0 look).\n\n**Public default stays `block` for everyone.**\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `renderSimpleLines` (bigfont) — scalable heavy box-drawing 7-segment font with\n  byte-for-byte width/height parity with `renderBigLines`, so the reserve-first\n  scaling and small-panel fallback thresholds are identical.\n- `renderOutlineLines` retained for the `outline` style; `DisplayStyle` enum gains\n  `\"outline\"`; `DISPLAY_STYLES` cycle = `block → simple → outline`.\n- `--bare`/`--zen` HUD collapses any non-`block` style to the compact single line\n  (scaled line fonts are a dashboard feature) — keeps small-terminal/zen behaviour.\n\n## Tests\n\n`renderSimpleLines` (dimensions, width parity, distinctness from block at scale 1,\ncolon dots, no-throw) + session-view `simple` and `outline` coverage. **534 passing**;\nbuild / typecheck / lint clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)"}]}
